# <type>[optional scope]: <description>
#
# [optional body]
#
# [optional footer(s)]
#
# --- Conventional Commits cheat sheet (release-please reads these) ---
# type:
#   feat     - new role / new variable / new behavior      -> minor bump
#   fix      - bugfix, no new behavior                      -> patch bump
#   chore    - tooling, CI, non-release-relevant changes     -> no bump
#   docs     - README/CHANGELOG/comments only                -> no bump
#   refactor - internal restructuring, no behavior change    -> no bump
#   test     - test-only changes                             -> no bump
#
# Breaking change: add "!" after type/scope, e.g. "feat!: ..."
# or add a footer "BREAKING CHANGE: <description>"           -> major bump
#
# scope (optional): the role or area affected, e.g.
#   feat(linux_os_updates): add reboot-window variable
#
# First line <= 72 chars, imperative mood ("add", not "added"/"adds").
